gametitle=Way of the Samurai 2 (NTSC-U) SLUS-20893 158FA006 (Undub)

[60 FPS]
author=heavyjam
description=Presents a frame every field instead of every second one, taking the game from 30 to 60 fps, and keeps it running at its normal speed. Way of the Samurai 2 steps its world once per presented frame with nothing measuring real time, so unlocking the frame rate on its own runs everything at double speed. Two more words correct that: the engine's frames-per-second constant goes from 30 to 60, which keeps every frame-counted timer (dialogue, events, the story clock) at the same wall-clock length, and every animation clock advances half a frame per step instead of a whole one, which keeps walking, running, combat and NPCs at their original pace because characters move with their animations. A 3-second walk covers the same ground at 60 fps as at 30. Things stepped per frame outside the animation system, such as camera easing and screen fades, complete in half the time. Costs twice the drawing per second. Applied at boot, so restart the game after ticking it.
patch=0,EE,001e1c34,word,240b0001
patch=0,EE,002eda00,word,0000003c
patch=0,EE,00137738,word,3c023f00
